"Tutorial text" = "
Use the always hidden feature to keep your icons tidy. Here's how to set it up:
Steps to enable:
1. Enable the always hidden “|” (translucent color bar).
2. Hold  ⌘ and drag it to the left-hand side of the normal bar, then move any icons you want to disappear to the left of that bar.
3. Finally, right-click the collapse “<” icon to make them disappear.
Steps to view always hidden icons:
1. Right-click the “<” icon again to view them, and repeat the action to hide them. Enjoy 😉!
